step Bodley
  when group 9015
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Bodley's ghost stands on the ledge before the Blackrock Spire portal, high inside Blackrock Mountain. Three Kings of Flame needs the Incendicite of Incendius (Lord Incendius, Blackrock Depths), the Ember of Emberseer (Pyroguard Emberseer, Upper Blackrock Spire), the Cinder of Cynders (Duke of Cynders, Silithus) and a Hallowed Brazier from the Argent Dawn.
  use 22115 @32.2,25.8 map 1428
  turnin 8960 only Alliance
  turnin 9032 only Horde

step Three Kings of Flame
  when group 8961
  zone Burning Steppes
  level 59
  accept 8961

step Honored with the Argent Dawn
  when onquest 8961
  when !rep "Argent Dawn" Honored
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip The Hallowed Brazier is sold only at Honored. With the Argent Dawn Commission worn, Scourge drop Scourgestones that the Argent officers accept for reputation; every Scourge kill in the Plaguelands counts, Stratholme and Scholomance undead give 5 each up to Honored, and Light's Hope Chapel dungeon quests give 100-200 each.
  equip 12846 optional            -- Argent Dawn Commission, while you fight the Scourge
  rep 529 Honored

step Hallowed Brazier
  when onquest 8961
  zone Eastern Plaguelands
  tip The Argent Dawn quartermasters (Light's Hope Chapel, Chillwind Camp, the Bulwark) sell it: 133 gold 33 silver, less with your reputation discount.
  buy 22014 nearest

step Blackrock Depths and Upper Blackrock Spire
  when group 8961
  zone Searing Gorge
  tip Lord Incendius guards the Black Anvil in Blackrock Depths (a group of five). Pyroguard Emberseer is the first boss of Upper Blackrock Spire, a group of up to ten. Each player with the quest loots their own.
  level 59
  kill 9017 @34.8,85.3 live group 5  -- Lord Incendius, Blackrock Depths
  collect 21987 quest 8961.1 @34.8,85.3 live
  kill 9816 @34.8,85.3 live group 10  -- Pyroguard Emberseer, Upper Blackrock Spire
  collect 21988 quest 8961.2 @34.8,85.3 live

step The Duke of Cynders
  when group 8961
  zone Silithus
  tip The Duke (level 62 elite, bring a group of five) only comes when someone summons him at one of the Twilight's Greater Wind Stones in Silithus: the summoner wears the full Twilight Cultist set (Cowl, Mantle and Robe, from the Twilight cultists of the Silithus camps), carries a Twilight Cultist Medallion of Station (Aurel Goldleaf at Cenarion Hold: three Abyssal Crests from summoned Templars and a Large Brilliant Shard) and a Signet of Beckoning: Fire, which calls the Duke of Cynders rather than a random Duke. Joining someone else's summon is the quick way: every player with the quest loots their own Cinder.
  level 60
  kill 15206 group 5  -- The Duke of Cynders
  collect 21989 quest 8961.3

